Web::Plain
==========

Flask-like routes and a small HTTP server for behind nginx, in plain Perl: routes are functions in a table,
requests plain hashes, responses plain arrays. No objects and no dependencies beyond core Perl.

    use Web::Plain;

    get  '/health'      => sub { { ok => 1 } };
    get  '/hello/:name' => sub { my ($req) = @_; "Hello, $req->{params}{name}!" };
    post '/echo'        => sub { my ($req) = @_; json($req->{json}, 201) };
    get  '/events'      => sub {
        stream(200, ['Content-Type' => 'text/event-stream'], sub {
            my ($write) = @_;
            $write->(sse({ n => $_ })) or return for 1 .. 3;
        });
    };
    run(listen => '/run/app/app.sock', mode => 0660);

The server listens on a unix socket, serves one request at a time and leaves TLS, keep-alive, slow clients
and limits to nginx in front of it (proxy_pass http://unix:/run/app/app.sock; proxy_buffering off for
streams). It suits a process that holds one expensive resource, such as a model on a GPU.

INSTALLATION

    perl Makefile.PL
    make
    make test
    make install

